{"content":[{"c":["ABISHAI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["David’s nephew, son of Zeruiah (by an unnamed father) and brother of Joab and Asahel (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.16","r":"1Chr.2.16","rawR":"1Chr.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.16","value":"1Chr.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:16"},"). Abishai volunteered to accompany David to Saul’s camp one night and would have killed the sleeping Saul if David had not restrained him (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.26.6-12","r":"1Sam.26.6-12","rawR":"1Sam.26.6-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.26.6-12","value":"1Sam.26.6-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 26:6-12"},"). He also helped Joab kill Abner, Saul’s general, in revenge for the death of another brother (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.3.30","r":"2Sam.3.30","rawR":"2Sam.3.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.3.30","value":"2Sam.3.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 3:30"},"). Later Abishai won a victory over the Edomites (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.18.12-13","r":"1Chr.18.12-13","rawR":"1Chr.18.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.18.12-13","value":"1Chr.18.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 18:12-13"},") and was second in command in a decisive battle against the Ammonites (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.19.10-15","r":"1Chr.19.10-15","rawR":"1Chr.19.10-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.19.10-15","value":"1Chr.19.10-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 19:10-15"},"). Often vengeful and cruel, Abishai wanted to behead the spiteful Shimei during Absalom’s rebellion, but again David intervened (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.16.5-12","r":"2Sam.16.5-12","rawR":"2Sam.16.5-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.16.5-12","value":"2Sam.16.5-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 16:5-12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.19.21-23","r":"2Sam.19.21-23","rawR":"2Sam.19.21-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.19.21-23","value":"2Sam.19.21-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:21-23"},"). When King David fled beyond the Jordan, Abishai was given command of one of David’s three divisions that crushed the rebellion (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.18.1-15","r":"2Sam.18.1-15","rawR":"2Sam.18.1-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.18.1-15","value":"2Sam.18.1-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 18:1-15"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In a later battle with the Philistines, Abishai saved David’s life by killing the giant Ishbi-benob (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.15-17","r":"2Sam.21.15-17","rawR":"2Sam.21.15-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.15-17","value":"2Sam.21.15-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21:15-17"},"). He ranked among David’s bravest warriors (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.18-19","r":"2Sam.23.18-19","rawR":"2Sam.23.18-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.18-19","value":"2Sam.23.18-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:18-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.20-21","r":"1Chr.11.20-21","rawR":"1Chr.11.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.20-21","value":"1Chr.11.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:20-21"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abishai","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.16","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.16","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 26:6-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.26.6-12","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.26.6-12","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.26.6-12"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 3:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.3.30","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.3.30","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.3.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 18:12-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.18.12-13","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.18.12-13","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.18.12-13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 19:10-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.19.10-15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.19.10-15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.19.10-15"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 16:5-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.16.5-12","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.16.5-12","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.16.5-12"},{"anchorText":"19:21-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.19.21-23","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.19.21-23","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.19.21-23"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 18:1-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.18.1-15","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.18.1-15","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.18.1-15"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 21:15-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.15-17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.15-17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.15-17"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:18-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.18-19","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.18-19","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.18-19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.20-21","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.20-21","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.20-21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6b598122836ed2f4925912a85dd279bd5b3574903f542958d580734be0b77d64","sourceItemName":"Abishai","sourceItemOrder":52,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Abishai","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Abishai","title":"Abishai","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}